        "Local routes start close by. M.J.P. Rohilkhand University in Bareilly has about 80 affiliated colleges, and the Indian Veterinary Research Institute at Izzatnagar is a national name in its field. Beyond the district, families think of Lucknow, Delhi, Aligarh, Kanpur and Roorkee, and of Pantnagar for agriculture. Students from IB or IGCSE backgrounds should read each institution's conditions for other-board applicants.",
        "Nationally, the Association of Indian Universities issues equivalence for the IB Diploma and for IGCSE-based qualifications, and many institutions ask to see it. CUET-UG is open to students of any board and is the main gateway to central universities. JEE and NEET-UG publish their own rules on subjects and marks in each year's information bulletin, which is the only reliable source.",
        "Uttar Pradesh runs its own counselling for engineering and medical seats, with eligibility notes that can differ for students from other boards. Read the current brochure from the counselling authority well before results, and ask a tutor to map subject choices onto those rules early, while a change of subject is still possible.",
        "Abroad, predicted grades open doors. British universities make conditional offers in IB points or A Level grades with subject minimums, American colleges weigh essays and activities too, and other countries publish conversion tables. Tutors raise the grades an application rests on; they do not write statements or run counselling.",
