        "The tier decides how high a grade can go. Core papers cap the top grade, whereas Extended opens the full scale. A student who may later enter the IB Diploma or aim at engineering should take Extended in Maths and the sciences, because that content is the foundation the Diploma assumes. A student unsure of Maths can start with Core and review after a first set of mocks.",
        "Board choice is practical. Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel are equally recognised, but they word questions differently, publish different mark schemes and run exams in different months. Decide which suits your timetable and nearest centre, then use only that board's past papers; mixing them leaves a student practising against the wrong style.",
